# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch's algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritmo de Deutsch"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves the parity problem for the special case that $n = 1$.\n"
"In the context of quantum computing this problem is sometimes referred to as *Deutsch's problem*, and we'll follow that nomenclature in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"O algoritmo de Deutsch resolve o problema de paridade para o caso especial em que $n = 1$.\n"
"No contexto da computação quântica, esse problema é às vezes chamado de *problema de Deutsch*, e seguiremos essa nomenclatura nesta lição.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, the input is represented by a function $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ from one bit to one bit.\n"
"There are four such functions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ser preciso, a entrada é representada por uma função $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ de um bit para um bit.\n"
"Existem quatro funções desse tipo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first and last of these functions are *constant* and the middle two are *balanced*, meaning that the two possible output values for the function occur the same number of times as we range over the inputs.\n"
"Deutsch's problem is to determine which of these two categories the input function belongs to: constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"A primeira e a última dessas funções são *constantes*, e as duas do meio são *balanceadas*, o que significa que os dois possíveis valores de saída da função ocorrem o mesmo número de vezes conforme variamos as entradas.\n"
"O problema de Deutsch consiste em determinar a qual dessas duas categorias a função de entrada pertence: constante ou balanceada.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch's problem\">\n"
"Input:  a function $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problema de Deutsch\">\n"
"Entrada:  uma função $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Saída: $0$ se $f$ é constante, $1$ se $f$ é balanceada\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we view the input function $f$ in Deutsch's problem as representing random access to a string, we're thinking about a two-bit string: $f(0)f(1)$.\n"
msgstr "Se interpretarmos a função de entrada $f$ no problema de Deutsch como representando acesso aleatório a uma string, estamos pensando em uma string de dois bits: $f(0)f(1).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When viewed in this way, Deutsch's problem is to compute the parity (or, equivalently, the exclusive-OR) of the two bits.\n"
msgstr "Visto dessa forma, o problema de Deutsch consiste em calcular a paridade (ou, equivalentemente, o OU-exclusivo) dos dois bits.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every classical query algorithm that correctly solves this problem must query both bits: $f(0)$ and $f(1)$.\n"
"If we learn that $f(1) = 1$, for instance, the answer could still be $0$ or $1$, depending on whether $f(0) = 1$ or $f(0) = 0$, respectively.\n"
"Every other case is similar; knowing just one of two bits doesn't provide any information at all about their parity.\n"
"So, the Boolean circuit described in the previous section is the best we can do in terms of the number of queries required to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Todo algoritmo de consulta clássico que resolve corretamente esse problema precisa consultar os dois bits: $f(0)$ e $f(1).$\n"
"Se soubermos que $f(1) = 1,$ por exemplo, a resposta ainda pode ser $0$ ou $1$, dependendo se $f(0) = 1$ ou $f(0) = 0$, respectivamente.\n"
"Todo outro caso é semelhante; conhecer apenas um dos dois bits não fornece nenhuma informação sobre a paridade deles.\n"
"Portanto, o circuito booleano descrito na seção anterior é o melhor que podemos fazer em termos do número de consultas necessárias para resolver esse problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit description {#quantum-circuit-description}"
msgstr "Descrição do circuito quântico {#quantum-circuit-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves Deutsch's problem using a single query, therefore providing a quantifiable advantage of quantum over classical computations.\n"
"This may be a modest advantage — one query as opposed to two — but we have to start somewhere.\n"
"Scientific advances sometimes have seemingly humble origins.\n"
msgstr ""
"O algoritmo de Deutsch resolve o problema de Deutsch usando uma única consulta, fornecendo assim uma vantagem quantificável da computação quântica sobre a clássica.\n"
"Essa pode ser uma vantagem modesta — uma consulta em vez de duas — mas precisamos começar em algum lugar.\n"
"Avanços científicos às vezes têm origens aparentemente modestas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit that describes Deutsch's algorithm:\n"
msgstr "Aqui está um circuito quântico que descreve o algoritmo de Deutsch:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Algoritmo de Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Análise {#analysis}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To analyze Deutsch's algorithm, we will trace through the action of the circuit above and identify the states of the qubits at the times suggested by this figure:\n"
msgstr "Para analisar o algoritmo de Deutsch, vamos percorrer a ação do circuito acima e identificar os estados dos qubits nos momentos sugeridos por esta figura:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![States during Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Estados durante o algoritmo de Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state is $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, and the two Hadamard operations on the left-hand side of the circuit transform this state to\n"
msgstr "O estado inicial é $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, e as duas operações de Hadamard no lado esquerdo do circuito transformam esse estado em\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(As always, we're following Qiskit's qubit ordering convention, which puts the top qubit to the right and the bottom qubit to the left.) It may feel unintuitive to write this product state partly distributed (leaving the states of qubit 1 factored out), but this will make our later expressions more compact.\n"
msgstr "(Como sempre, seguimos a convenção de ordenação de qubits do Qiskit, que coloca o qubit do topo à direita e o qubit de baixo à esquerda.) Pode parecer pouco intuitivo escrever esse estado de produto parcialmente distribuído (deixando os estados do qubit 1 fatorados fora), mas isso tornará nossas expressões posteriores mais compactas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"According to the definition of the $U_f$ gate, the value of the function $f$ for the classical state of the top/rightmost qubit is XORed onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, which transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, a porta $U_f$ é aplicada.\n"
"De acordo com a definição da porta $U_f$, o valor da função $f$ para o estado clássico do qubit do topo/mais à direita é aplicado via XOR no qubit de baixo/mais à esquerda, o que transforma $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ no estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can simplify this expression by observing that the formula\n"
msgstr "Podemos simplificar essa expressão observando que a fórmula\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"works for both possible values $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"More explicitly, the two cases are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"é válida para ambos os possíveis valores $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"De forma mais explícita, os dois casos são os seguintes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we can alternatively express $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ like this:\n"
msgstr "Assim, podemos expressar $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ alternativamente da seguinte forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Something interesting just happened!\n"
"Although the action of the $U_f$ gate on standard basis states leaves the top/rightmost qubit alone and XORs the function value onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, here we see that the state of the top/rightmost qubit has changed (in general) while the state of the bottom/leftmost qubit remains the same — specifically being in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state before and after the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"This phenomenon is known as the *phase kickback*, and we will have more to say about it shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algo interessante acabou de acontecer!\n"
"Embora a ação da porta $U_f$ sobre estados da base padrão deixe o qubit do topo/mais à direita intacto e aplique o XOR do valor da função no qubit de baixo/mais à esquerda, aqui vemos que o estado do qubit do topo/mais à direita mudou (em geral), enquanto o estado do qubit de baixo/mais à esquerda permanece o mesmo — especificamente no estado $\\vert - \\rangle$ antes e depois da aplicação da porta $U_f$.\n"
"Esse fenômeno é conhecido como *phase kickback* (retrocesso de fase), e falaremos mais sobre ele em breve.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With one final simplification, which is to pull the factor of $(-1)^{f(0)}$ outside of the sum, we obtain this expression of the state $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Com uma simplificação final, que consiste em extrair o fator $(-1)^{f(0)}$ para fora da soma, obtemos esta expressão para o estado $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{se $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{se $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that in this expression, we have $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ in the exponent of $-1$ as opposed to $f(1) - f(0)$, which is what we might expect from a purely algebraic viewpoint, but we obtain the same result either way.\n"
"This is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"Observe que nessa expressão temos $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ no expoente de $-1$, em vez de $f(1) - f(0)$, que seria o esperado de um ponto de vista puramente algébrico, mas obtemos o mesmo resultado de qualquer forma.\n"
"Isso ocorre porque o valor $(-1)^k$ para qualquer inteiro $k$ depende apenas de $k$ ser par ou ímpar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the final Hadamard gate to the top qubit leaves us with the state\n"
msgstr "Aplicando a porta de Hadamard final ao qubit do topo, chegamos ao estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{se $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{se $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which leads to the correct outcome with probability $1$ when the right/topmost qubit is measured.\n"
msgstr "o que leva ao resultado correto com probabilidade $1$ quando o qubit mais à direita/topo é medido.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Further remarks on the phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"
msgstr "Observações adicionais sobre o phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, let's look at the analysis above from a slightly different angle that may shed some light on the phase kickback phenomenon.\n"
msgstr "Antes de prosseguir, vamos analisar a discussão acima sob um ângulo ligeiramente diferente, o que pode lançar alguma luz sobre o fenômeno do phase kickback.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, notice that the following formula works for all choices of bits $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "Primeiro, observe que a seguinte fórmula é válida para todas as escolhas de bits $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be verified by checking it for the two possible values $c = 0$ and $c = 1$:\n"
msgstr "Isso pode ser verificado checando os dois possíveis valores $c = 0$ e $c = 1$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using this formula, we see that\n"
msgstr "Usando essa fórmula, vemos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every choice of bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Because this formula is true for $b=0$ and $b=1$, we see by linearity that\n"
msgstr ""
"para toda escolha de bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Como essa fórmula é verdadeira para $b=0$ e $b=1$, vemos por linearidade que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all qubit state vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, and therefore\n"
msgstr "para todos os vetores de estado de qubit $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, e portanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key that makes this work is that $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the vector $\\vert - \\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* of the matrix $X$ having *eigenvalue* $-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"A chave que faz isso funcionar é que $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"Em termos matemáticos, o vetor $\\vert - \\rangle$ é um *autovetor* da matriz $X$ com *autovalor* $-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll discuss eigenvectors and eigenvalues in greater detail in the upcoming lesson on *Phase estimation and factoring,* where the phase kickback phenomenon is generalized to other unitary operations.\n"
msgstr "Discutiremos autovetores e autovalores com mais detalhes na próxima lição sobre *Estimativa de fase e fatoração*, onde o fenômeno do phase kickback é generalizado para outras operações unitárias.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeping in mind that scalars float freely through tensor products, we find an alternative way of reasoning how the operation $U_f$ transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ in the analysis above:\n"
msgstr "Lembrando que escalares se propagam livremente pelos produtos tensoriais, encontramos uma forma alternativa de raciocinar sobre como a operação $U_f$ transforma $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ em $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ na análise acima:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation in Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"
msgstr "Implementação no Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how we can implement Deutsch's algorithm in Qiskit. We'll start with a version check and then perform the imports required solely for this implementation.\n"
"For the implementations of other algorithms that follows, we'll perform the required imports separately for the sake of greater modularity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora vamos ver como podemos implementar o algoritmo de Deutsch no Qiskit. Começaremos com uma verificação de versão e em seguida faremos as importações necessárias exclusivamente para esta implementação.\n"
"Para as implementações de outros algoritmos que se seguem, faremos as importações necessárias separadamente em prol de maior modularidade.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll define a quantum circuit that implements a query gate for one of the four functions $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, or $f_4$ from one bit to one bit described previously. As we already mentioned, the implementation of query gates is not really a part of Deutsch's algorithm itself;\n"
"here we're essentially just showing one way to prepare the input, in the form of a circuit implementation of a query gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro definiremos um circuito quântico que implementa uma porta de consulta para uma das quatro funções $f_1,$ $f_2,$ $f_3,$ ou $f_4$ de um bit para um bit descritas anteriormente. Como já mencionamos, a implementação de portas de consulta não é realmente parte do próprio algoritmo de Deutsch;\n"
"aqui estamos essencialmente mostrando uma maneira de preparar a entrada, na forma de uma implementação em circuito de uma porta de consulta.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see what each circuit looks like using the `draw` method. Here's the circuit for the function $f_3$.\n"
msgstr "Podemos ver como cada circuito se parece usando o método `draw`. Aqui está o circuito para a função $f_3$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will create the actual quantum circuit for Deutsch's algorithm, substituting the query gate with a quantum circuit implementation given as an argument. Shortly we'll plug in one of the four circuits defined by the function `deutsch_function` we defined earlier.\n"
"Barriers are included to show the visual separation between the query gate implementation and the rest of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, criaremos o circuito quântico real para o algoritmo de Deutsch, substituindo a porta de consulta por uma implementação em circuito quântico fornecida como argumento. Em breve, vamos conectar um dos quatro circuitos definidos pela função `deutsch_function` que definimos anteriormente.\n"
"Barreiras são incluídas para mostrar a separação visual entre a implementação da porta de consulta e o restante do circuito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again we can see what the circuit looks like using the `draw` method.\n"
msgstr "Novamente podemos ver como o circuito se parece usando o método `draw`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we'll create a function that runs the circuit previously defined one time and outputs the appropriate result: \"constant\" or \"balanced.\"\n"
msgstr "Por fim, criaremos uma função que executa o circuito definido anteriormente uma única vez e retorna o resultado apropriado: \"constant\" ou \"balanced.\"\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run Deutsch's algorithm on any one of the four functions defined above.\n"
msgstr "Agora podemos executar o algoritmo de Deutsch em qualquer uma das quatro funções definidas acima.\n"
